{
  "case_id": "2017-17-459",
  "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Section 1229(a)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Specifically, Section 1229(a) defines a notice to appear as notice that provides specific information, including the time and place at which proceedings will be held."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The stop-time rule at issue in this case specifies exactly what the government must do in order to end an immigrant's period of continuous presence. The government must serve a notice to appear under Section 1229(a), and as the name notice to appear suggests, the government cannot serve a notice to appear without telling an immigrant when and where to appear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Zimmer, you just said defines the notice of appear. Why do you think that those 10 requirements of what have to be in a notice to appear define a notice to appear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Former BIA Chairman Schmidt",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, in fact, this is explained in even more detail in the amicus brief submitted by former BIA chairman and Immigration Judge Schmidt, who -- who explains that this system allowed coordination between the Department of Homeland Security and the immigration courts, such that individual DHS officers could identify a time that could be included on the notice to appear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Zimmer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, yes, there's a big practical difference because, in a case like Camarillo, they're not trying to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "why -- why is one better for your client than the other?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Meaning -- so the start of your client's ability to force the government to give it a hearing doesn't start until it's filed in the immigration court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Zimmer, can I take you back to the language of the statute and just ask about your assertion that this is clearly definitional in nature?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A notice to appear that lacks a date and time is still a notice to appear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The reason why (A) through (D) are essential is because (A) through (D) are about -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Liu",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Congress actually told us in 1996 and then again in NACARA in 1997, and these provisions are at the statutory appendix at 69a.\nIn 1996, when Congress enacted this very statute, it said that the stop-time rule should apply to notices to appear issued before the effective date."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Mr. Liu, this might be the same question and, if so, I -- I apologize for beating you over the head with it, but a -- a notice to appear, it's a special kind of charging document. It's telling you that the government wants you to appear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the BIA recognized it was either/or: Either they were all required or none were required. And the BIA held that there were no substantive requirements on a notice to appear to trigger the stop-time rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But when he -- when he had notice that the government was going to attempt to remove him?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Zimmer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "362e695b0f41fbd8209dcbcb337c3c1aec8d7c2ec2609608e85059b2dae3b3e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-362e695b0f41-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "approximately 10 percent of notices to appear that are issued are never even filed in immigration court at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-17-459",
      "confidence": 0.0,
